Layer-streamed low-VRAM LoRA training (deep-apply streamed backend)
------------------------------------------------------------------
The streamed training backend (src/asea/deepapply/trainer.py,
``StreamedTrainerBackend``) implements the layer-streaming / offloading
technique published as **Soup** by MakazhanAlpamys:

    Repository : github.com/MakazhanAlpamys/Soup
    License    : Apache-2.0
    Demonstrated: training an 8B-parameter LoRA adapter in ~3.3 GB of VRAM by
                  keeping the frozen base in host RAM and streaming decoder
                  layers to the GPU one at a time, with LoRA params resident
                  on device.

This technique is third-party published work and is credited here, in the
backend's module docstring, and in docs/deep_apply_design.md. It is NOT claimed
as original work of this project. The backend name and version are recorded in
every AdapterPacket that the streamed backend produces, so the prior-art
provenance of a trained adapter is inspectable.

Deep-apply's standard backend (``StandardTrainerBackend``) is a conventional
PEFT/LoRA fine-tune (HuggingFace transformers + PEFT, Apache-2.0) and does not
use the Soup technique.

